  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advies en overige diensten</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 17 July 2026 the Municipality of Puerto El Carmen de Putumayo andHospital San Miguel &#x2013; Quina Care Foundation jointly requested the supportof the Dutch Disaster Risk Reduction &amp; Surge Support (DRRS) programme toaddress a rapidly worsening river erosion emergency threatening Puerto ElCarmen and its critical infrastructure.Since the Putumayo River changed course in 2010, severe riverbank erosionhas destroyed the town&apos;s riverbank protection, drinking water intake andvarious infrastructures along the river walkway. The erosion has now alsoreached the Hospital San Miguel grounds, where buildings have alreadycollapsed into the river, placing the main hospital building&#x2014;and the onlyhospital serving the border region&#x2014;at imminent risk.Given the urgency of the situation and the potential loss of essential servicesand parts of the town, DRRS support was requested to help assess thesituation and identify effective short- and long-term risk reductionmeasures. Discussions with the Municipality confirmed that sufficientfunding is a major barrier to address the erosion, underscoring the need forexternal support to help prioritize and realize effective action.</narrative>
  </description>
